# Security headers for the whole site. See https://docs.netlify.com/manage/routing/headers/
#
# Honest note on the Content-Security-Policy below: this site relies heavily on inline
# style="..." attributes and large inline <script> blocks throughout every page (that's how
# the whole thing is built — no separate .css/.js build step). A strict CSP that blocks inline
# code would break the site outright, so 'unsafe-inline' is included below. That measurably
# weakens what CSP can protect against (particularly XSS), but the alternative — a broken tool —
# isn't a real option without a much larger rebuild. connect-src is scoped to https: broadly
# rather than an exact per-API allowlist, since this tool calls 20+ different government data
# APIs and missing even one from a strict allowlist would silently break a live data source.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(self), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; connect-src 'self' https:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://buy.stripe.com
